    }
  },
  "ownScientificReasons": [
    "The actual RP page40 provides the three relevant derivative classes through its mandatory ester content plus explicit optional acid-anhydride and acid-chloride examples. This is a bounded named chemistry domain, rather than an arbitrary extension from generic competencies.",
    "The LK additum names the nucleophilic substitution addition-elimination mechanism. The optional block names carbonyl reactivity as a determinant of rate and equilibrium. A comparative acyl-substitution explanation connects these locally coherent source contents.",
    "Pages19-21 authorize selecting and concretizing optional deepening/networking content, while distinguishing it from obligatory Fundamentum/Additum. Pages12-15 support explaining mechanisms, using chemical-bond models, finding/explaining trends and scientifically coherent argument. They do not make the exact comparison a literal compulsory operator.",
    "Ranking acid chlorides, acid anhydrides and esters in comparable acyl-substitution cases is scientifically defensible using electrophilic carbonyl character and departure of the leaving group. The comparison must preserve reaction/nucleophile/substituent/conditions; it is not a universal rate statement over incomparable cases.",
    "The whole current DE/EN text contains this comparability guard and describes one complete comparative routine. No class needs to be silently removed and no unmatched extra lactone-stability duty is being promoted."
  ],
